WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.780
Is it really Westeros without dragons and kings?&nbsp;
The upcoming Game of Thrones spinoff The Hedge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.340
Knight might just give viewers an entirely&nbsp;
new perspective on life in the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:11.837
"I could tell you about Ser Duncan the&nbsp;
Tall. Those were always your favorites."

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.920
Game of Thrones had its fair share of really,&nbsp;
really tall characters. There's the Hound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.620
who in the books is said to measure in at 6 feet&nbsp;
8 inches. The actor who played him, Rory McCann,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.260
is a close 6 feet, 6 inches. Then there was his&nbsp;
brother, the Mountain, who was played by multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:35.220
actors, but most notably by Icelandic strongman&nbsp;
Hafþór Björnsson, who is 6 feet 9 inches. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.900
certainly above average for a man, the book's&nbsp;
iteration of the Mountain was even taller.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.820
Then, there was Brienne of Tarth, portrayed&nbsp;
by the 6-foot-3-inch Gwendoline Christie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.260
Martin describes her as about 6 and a&nbsp;
half feet. And who could forget Hodor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.380
the gentle giant brought to life by 6-foot-10-inch&nbsp;
actor Kristian Nairn, who held the door for Bran.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.580
The Hedge Knight will introduce another&nbsp;
person of preposterous stature to the Game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.980
of Thrones extended universe. The protagonist&nbsp;
and point-of-view character, Dunk, is so tall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:10.260
that instead of his family or place of birth,&nbsp;
his defining characteristic becomes his name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:17.220
Ser Duncan the Tall is reported to be nearly 7&nbsp;
feet by one account and exactly 6 feet, 11 inches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.860
by another. His size isn't just remarkable enough&nbsp;
to have been preserved in Westeros' history books;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.080
it's also a comedic contrast between Dunk and&nbsp;
his traveling companion, the diminutive Egg.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.300
Very few actors match Dunk's stats, and&nbsp;
productions usually use camera trickery and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.460
digital effects to create such illusions. Among&nbsp;
the fans' suggestions for Dunk are Henry Cavill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.280
and George MacKay. Both standing in the vicinity&nbsp;
of 6 feet in height, they're tall for movie stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:50.160
but not for knights. Since Ser Duncan's appearance&nbsp;
is so important to the story, many readers are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.080
hoping for a properly towering figure, which&nbsp;
might mean casting someone relatively unknown.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.200
Of all Martin's books, A Knight of the Seven&nbsp;
Kingdoms should be the easiest to adapt. Game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.300
of Thrones had to fit thousands of pages&nbsp;
of story into Seasons 1-5, while House of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.260
the Dragon uses only a tiny section of&nbsp;
Fire &amp; Blood for its first 10 episodes.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:15.420
Both had to contend with dozens of locations&nbsp;
and hundreds of characters. The Hedge Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.140
and its accompanying graphic novel, on&nbsp;
the other hand, are less than 200 pages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.300
and feature one main setting and a manageable&nbsp;
number of central players. This means that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.380
assuming the showrunners keep the book to a&nbsp;
single season, the show ought to be able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.700
render the events of the novella at about the&nbsp;
same pace and with the same amount of detail.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.480
But adaptations shouldn't be afraid&nbsp;
to make changes that improve the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.020
story for the new medium. One area&nbsp;
where the TV show could do better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.460
than the book is in its depiction of&nbsp;
Dunk's mentor, Ser Arlan of Pennytree.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.960
Arlan is an archetypical Game of&nbsp;
Thrones character: like Davos Seaworth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.220
he's an older nobleman and hardworking knight&nbsp;
with a grizzled appearance and demeanor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.720
good intentions, and a slightly&nbsp;
mysterious backstory. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.340
we never actually meet him in Martin's&nbsp;
writing, and some fans want the series to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.300
correct that. While some folks on Reddit&nbsp;
have suggested starting the show with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.800
Ser Arlan, others think Ser Arlan and Dunk's&nbsp;
relationship could be handled in flashbacks.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.480
Family words and crests play a vital&nbsp;
part in the overall aesthetic and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.320
narrative of Game of Thrones. There&nbsp;
are also many ancestral weapons like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.500
swords and shields that mean a&nbsp;
great deal to various characters.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.373
"See that sword? It's called Heartsbane."

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.620
Ser Duncan's shield serves as the cover of some&nbsp;
editions of A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:39.360
it's a major Easter egg that supposedly connects&nbsp;
Dunk to a beloved major character down the line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.580
though fans have yet to discover exactly how.&nbsp;
In all likelihood, viewers of The Hedge Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.020
will get to see the origin story behind&nbsp;
that shield and its design early in Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:53.580
1. The ultimate reveal, however, probably&nbsp;
won't come until closer to the show's end.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.760
When Dunk comes into possession&nbsp;
of Ser Arlan's belongings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.920
he realizes that since he isn't Arlan's&nbsp;
son, he cannot use the Pennytree's symbol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:07.140
or colors — a winged silver chalice against&nbsp;
a brown backdrop. The problem is that Dunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.940
isn't anybody's son. He was orphaned in his&nbsp;
infancy and knows nothing about his heritage.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:17.460
To become a respected-enough hedge knight to enter&nbsp;
tournaments and find work, he basically has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:22.800
invent an identity for himself. How plausible&nbsp;
that identity is, both to Dunk and to noble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.480
outside observers, is one of the main catalysts&nbsp;
of the action in A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.440
The way in which Dunk comes by his&nbsp;
new personal coat of arms is one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.940
of the book's more captivating subplots.&nbsp;
The image — an elm tree under a shooting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.200
star — is quite beautiful and sure&nbsp;
to adorn tons of official merch.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:47.160
Besides dragons, palace intrigue, violence,&nbsp;
and frozen zombies, Game of Thrones is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.420
known for its steamy romances. A cursory&nbsp;
glance through the history of Westeros&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:56.520
relationships will reveal that most of them are&nbsp;
complicated, if not utterly doomed from the start.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:02.040
If The Hedge Knight hews closely to the text at&nbsp;
all, Dunk will have his very own fraught subplot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:07.740
with a love interest, and it's one that some fans&nbsp;
of the novella are deeply invested in. When he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.080
arrives at the tournament at Ashford, Ser Duncan&nbsp;
makes the acquaintance of Tanselle, a Dornish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:18.120
artist and puppeteer who goes from town to town&nbsp;
with her uncle as part of a troupe of performers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.980
Dunk can't get the statuesque Tanselle —&nbsp;
whose nickname is Too-Tall — out of his mind.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:27.840
Even those who haven't read the book can probably&nbsp;
guess how things go for Dunk and Tanselle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.220
based only on the premise that they both&nbsp;
lead somewhat transient lifestyles and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.120
Martin's tendency to rip lovers apart&nbsp;
as soon as he gets them together.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:42.060
The fates of iconic couples like Daenerys&nbsp;
and Drogo, Robb Stark and Talisa, Jon Snow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:47.040
and Ygritte, Jaime Lannister and Brienne,&nbsp;
Missandei and Grey Worm, and Jon Snow and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.180
Daenerys still pull at the heartstrings&nbsp;
of many viewers. But that's not the point.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.520
The point is, Martin's best pairings crackle with&nbsp;
tension, particularly before they get together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:02.340
Dunk doesn't have Tyrion's wit or Jaime's charm,&nbsp;
but he's as much a lover as he is a fighter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.780
and The Hedge Knight should let his chivalrous&nbsp;
lead fall hard enough for Tanselle that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.380
has something to think about as he&nbsp;
wanders Westeros in later seasons.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.980
There's a ancient saying&nbsp;
about the Targaryen dynasty:

00:06:14.149 --> 00:06:19.909
"They say every time a Targaryen is born, the&nbsp;
gods toss a coin and the world holds its breath."

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:25.080
The two sides of this allegorical coin&nbsp;
are greatness and madness. Dunk and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.040
audiences will come into contact with&nbsp;
a whole new generation of Targaryens in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.820
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms, and&nbsp;
that coin flip wisdom will hold up.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:37.920
At court around the time of Ser Duncan are&nbsp;
Prince Maekar and Prince Baelor Breakspear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:44.700
as well as Maekar's sons, the Princes Daeron,&nbsp;
Aerion, Aemon, and Aegon. Daeron goes down in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.920
history as Daeron the Drunken. He's plagued by&nbsp;
prophetic dreams and self-medicates with drink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.780
and women to ease his mind. He's no peach,&nbsp;
but his fellow prince Aerion is much worse.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:59.220
Aerion, who calls himself Brightflame, will&nbsp;
probably function as the main antagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.960
in The Hedge Knight. As Targaryens go, he&nbsp;
doesn't inflict the worst or the most damage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:08.640
though he's still completely vile and cruel.&nbsp;
He's in the running for most mad, however.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:13.500
This vicious prince is really into&nbsp;
his family's history with dragons — so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.220
much so that he eventually believes&nbsp;
himself to be one. Aerion decorates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.300
his clothing to approximate the look&nbsp;
of a dragon and dabbles in dark magic.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.120
To compare his character&nbsp;
to another fantasy series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.260
he's like a combination of Gilderoy&nbsp;
Lockhart crossed with Voldemort from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:32.640
Harry Potter. He's the antithesis of&nbsp;
Dunk, who's kind and self-deprecating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:37.980
If HBO Max's The Hedge Knight gets their&nbsp;
rivalry right, the series should be a hit.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:43.020
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms takes place&nbsp;
almost exactly in between House of the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:48.420
and Game of Thrones. Dragons existed during&nbsp;
those series, but sadly, they're extinct in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:53.520
Dunk and Egg's age. Will casual viewers still&nbsp;
tune in for a dragon-less fantasy show? Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.080
fans don't think it'll be a problem thanks&nbsp;
to another massive spectacle — tournaments!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.400
While duels and jousting might not sound&nbsp;
especially enticing to fans used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:07.680
seeing enormous monsters on screen, without CGI&nbsp;
dragons taking a bite out of production budgets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.520
that money can go toward making&nbsp;
Season 1's tournaments extra grand.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.380
Of course, there have been several tournaments&nbsp;
in series set in Westeros already. On Game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:21.240
of Thrones, Robert, Joffrey, and Renly&nbsp;
Baratheon all hold tourneys. For its part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.260
House of the Dragon's premier episode&nbsp;
showcases Viserys Targaryen's tournament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:28.860
intended to celebrate the birth&nbsp;
of his and Aemma's son with one.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:33.540
Since several prominent tales in A Knight of&nbsp;
the Seven Kingdoms take place at tourneys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:38.040
this should mean they'll take center stage in&nbsp;
the television adaptation. If done correctly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:43.140
instead of montages of jousting and swordplay,&nbsp;
The Hedge Knight ought to show the tourney in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:47.040
full and allow the audience to get&nbsp;
to know and care about each entrant.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:53.400
Westeros isn't exactly an egalitarian society.&nbsp;
There's a ruling class and a working class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.300
and they're unmistakably distinct&nbsp;
from each other. Though being of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.980
noble birth comes with its challenges, it's&nbsp;
no picnic being a servant at King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.620
let alone a peasant on the streets of Flea Bottom.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:09.840
One of the few contexts in which the landed&nbsp;
gentry and the common folk mix? Live theater!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.752 --> 00:09:14.520
Mummers troupes often perform lewd versions&nbsp;
of royal history in the world of Thrones for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:20.100
the rich and the poor alike. For example, Teenage&nbsp;
Rhaenyra gets a taste of local politics when her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:24.180
uncle Daemon takes her on a late-night field&nbsp;
trip to witness a roast of her own family.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:29.580
As previously mentioned, Tanselle is a member of a&nbsp;
troupe of puppeteers that's assembled to entertain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.380
the crowds gathered for the tourney. That troupe&nbsp;
puts on what turns out to be quite a controversial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:40.260
and consequential show with marionette-like wooden&nbsp;
dragons. While it upsets characters in-world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.400
the show's potential audience in our world&nbsp;
should get excited to see them acted out.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:49.740
The creators of Game of Thrones and House of the&nbsp;
Dragon have done an exemplary job already with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:54.240
these types of stories within stories. Tanselle's&nbsp;
puppet show is yet another chance for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.319
cast and crew of The Hedge Knight to get creative&nbsp;
putting their own spin on a franchise tradition.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:03.180
Just as the citizens of Westeros&nbsp;
don't enjoy income equality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:07.560
they also can't depend on a very fair&nbsp;
legal system. For those suspected of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:13.002
a crime in Martin's world, the choice is often&nbsp;
between corporal punishment or trial by combat.

00:10:13.002 --> 00:10:16.182
"I demand a Trial by Combat."

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:20.220
Game of Thrones fans have been present&nbsp;
for some marquee trials by combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:24.540
mostly involving Tyrion Lannister. Bronn&nbsp;
fights on his behalf the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.220
Oberyn Martell the second. These scenes are&nbsp;
some of the highlights of the whole series.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:34.440
Without giving too much away, Dunk finds himself&nbsp;
in a similar position at some point during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.880
the events of A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.&nbsp;
Fortunately, he's more than capable of defending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:44.040
himself. Unfortunately, his adversary demands&nbsp;
a Trial by Seven, in which both the accuser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:48.540
and the accused must assemble a team of seven&nbsp;
to square off in what amounts to a mega-duel.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:53.400
This is easier said than done for Dunk, who&nbsp;
isn't highborn and doesn't have a Lannister's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:58.200
money or connections. The Trial by Seven is&nbsp;
the climax of The Hedge Knight and fans on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.860
Twitter are losing their minds about the&nbsp;
possibility of seeing it in live action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.340
It will be the first time book readers&nbsp;
will see a Trial by Seven on screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:08.820
with each knight battling with his&nbsp;
choice of fighting style and weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:13.263
and it will put a number of the show's main&nbsp;
characters in a life-or-death situation.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.900
If all goes well, The Hedge Knight could comprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.080
the first of at least three seasons&nbsp;
of A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:23.760
While there are some recognizable tie-ins to&nbsp;
the author's overarching story in part one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.740
most of the stuff fans are really waiting to see&nbsp;
won't happen until much later in Dunk's life.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:33.600
Ser Duncan plays a pivotal role in the&nbsp;
Blackfyre Rebellions. He's rumored to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:37.080
have fathered at least one child and is&nbsp;
thought to be related to at least one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:40.620
fan-favorite Game of Thrones character.&nbsp;
He even crosses paths with the likes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:45.540
A Song of Ice and Fire veterans Walder&nbsp;
Frey, Barristan Selmy, and Maester Aemon.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:50.760
Though Dunk's tale is relatively modest in scope&nbsp;
and length, it offers a fresh perspective into key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:55.620
pieces of Martin's lore. Not to mention, Ser&nbsp;
Duncan the Tall becomes a legendary knight in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.620 --> 00:12:00.000
his own regard. We don't know if A Knight of the&nbsp;
Seven Kingdoms will stop where the novellas do as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.100
of now or if Martin and Max will explore Westeros&nbsp;
through Dunk's eyes beyond "The Mystery Knight."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:09.900
But we can hope that if "The Hedge Knight" is&nbsp;
successful, this series and other spin offs could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:14.460
eventually give fans live-action adaptations&nbsp;
of more of their favorite book moments.

